# Extra patterns for the redaction check (one regular expression per line).
# The workflow passes this file as the scanner's `patterns-file`.

# A Claude Code project directory name. Claude Code names each project's
# folder under `.claude/projects/` after the absolute path of the workspace,
# with the separators turned into dashes, so a literal name gives away the
# machine layout just as an absolute path does. Samples use `<workspace-id>`.
# Matches the name after `projects` whether the path is written in one string
# or joined from quoted parts, in the Windows form (a drive letter and two
# dashes) and the Unix form (a leading dash and two or more parts).
projects["']?\s*[/\\,]+\s*["']?(?:[A-Za-z]--[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*|-[A-Za-z0-9._]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9._]+)+)
